D2. Weave identity (PROVED, one line).  For u in [0,1) the two preimages of u under
    t -> 2t are u/2 and u/2 + 1/2; even speeds 2e give ||e u|| at both, and for odd o
    ||o(u/2 + 1/2)|| = 1/2 - ||o u/2||.  Hence
      delta(v) = max_u min{ f_{E/2}(u),  max( min_o ||o u/2||,  1/2 - max_o ||o u/2|| ) }.
    Consequences: delta(O) = 1/2 for every nonempty set O of odd speeds (t = 1/2, i.e. u = 0
    on the shifted branch),
    so 'delta of the odd part' carries no information, and (I1) reads delta(v) <= delta(E/2).

    Census test of (I1)-(I4):
